# Generated. Regenerate with `pnpm test:ec`, never hand-edit.
docs/EDGE_CASES.md

# Generated by `apps/vi/tests/test_constraint_shapes.py` from the pinned library at test time.
#
# Two formatters fighting over one file: prettier reformats it, the pytest run rewrites it in its own
# shape, and `pnpm format:check` fails on a file nobody hand-edited. Generated means generated — the
# Python side owns its formatting, exactly as it owns its content.
apps/vi/tests/constraint_shapes.json

# The specification itself.
#
# It is the authoritative source of truth: it is quoted by section number in hundreds of comments, its
# line numbers are recorded in `docs/edge-cases.json` (`specLine`), and it is the input to
# `scripts/gen-edge-cases.mjs`. Reformatting it would produce a ~1,700-line diff, move every recorded
# line number, and risk mangling a table that the whole project parses. It is also not our prose.
docs/spec/countersign-blueprint.md

# The judge panel's verdict, reproduced verbatim.
#
# Same reasoning as the spec, and one more: this is the document the work is being held to. Reformatting
# the reviewer's own words so they match our style is a small thing that reads as editing the review.
# Prettier also cannot settle on it — `--write` leaves it still failing `--check`.
docs/review/VERDICT.md

# Markdown tables in the decision log and the status table are hand-aligned for readability; Prettier
# reflows them and the result is a whole-file diff on every one-line status change, which is the
# opposite of what a log that gets read on every work package is for.
docs/DECISIONS.md
docs/PROGRESS.md

# Generated by `scripts/gen-walkthrough.mjs` from a **running** app, never hand-edited.
#
# The file embeds six pages' real server-rendered markup verbatim. Prettier reformats that markup, which
# both rewrites the product's own output and produces a 70 KB diff on every regeneration — and the whole
# point of generating it is that regenerating is cheap. `scripts/gen-walkthrough.mjs` owns its shape.
docs/walkthrough.html